#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:3
msgid "损失函数"
msgstr "Loss Functions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:5
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{ref}`task-"
"formulations`中我们讨论了分类、回归、自回归三类任务的数学形式。不同任务需要不同的方式量化\"预测好坏\"——这就是损失函数的作用。"
msgstr ""
"In {ref}`task-formulations`, we discussed the mathematical formulations of classification, regression, and autoregression tasks. Different tasks require different ways to quantify \"prediction quality\"—which is precisely the role of loss functions."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:7
msgid "损失函数的本质：定义优化目标"
msgstr "Essence of Loss Functions: Defining the Optimization Goal"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"损失函数衡量模型预测与真实值之间的差异，将训练转化为**优化问题**。不同的任务类型对应不同的损失函数，塑造了不同的**损失曲面几何**，影响{ref"
"}`gradient-descent`优化的难易程度。"
msgstr ""
"A loss function measures the discrepancy between model predictions and true targets, transforming training into an **optimization problem**. Different task types correspond to different loss functions, shaping distinct **loss surface geometries** that affect the difficulty of optimization via {ref}`gradient-descent`."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:12
msgid "损失函数定义误差曲面"
msgstr "Loss Functions Define Error Surfaces"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:59
msgid "**核心作用**："
msgstr "**Core Roles**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:61
msgid "**量化误差**：将预测好坏转化为可计算的数值"
msgstr "**Quantifying error**: Converts prediction quality into a computable numeric value"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:62
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**指导优化**：通过梯度告诉模型\"如何调整\"（详见{ref}`gradient-descent`）"
msgstr "**Guiding optimization**: Instructs the model \"how to adjust\" via gradients (see {ref}`gradient-descent` for details)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:63
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**塑造曲面**：不同损失函数对应不同的{ref}`gradient-descent`优化难度"
msgstr "**Shaping the landscape**: Different loss functions correspond to different optimization difficulties for {ref}`gradient-descent`"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:67
msgid "回归问题的损失函数"
msgstr "Loss Functions for Regression Problems"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:69
msgid "均方误差（MSE）"
msgstr "Mean Squared Error (MSE)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:71
msgid "对大错误\"零容忍\""
msgstr "\"Zero Tolerance\" for Large Errors"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:73
msgid "想象你在玩飞镖。如果你投得离靶心很近，误差很小，这没问题。但如果你投偏了很远，平方误差会让这个错误**显得特别大**——就像老师批改作业时，小错误扣1分，但大错误要扣10分。"
msgstr "Imagine playing darts. If you throw very close to the bullseye, the error is small, which is fine. But if you miss by a wide margin, squared error makes this mistake **look exceptionally large**—much like a teacher deducting 1 point for a minor error but 10 points for a major blunder."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:75
msgid ""
"**为什么平方？** "
"因为平方让大的偏差被放大。误差为2时，惩罚是4；误差为4时，惩罚是16。这种\"零容忍大错误\"的特性让模型特别关注那些预测很离谱的样本。"
msgstr ""
"**Why square?** Because squaring amplifies large deviations. When the error is 2, the penalty is 4; when the error is 4, the penalty jumps to 16. This \"zero tolerance for large errors\" property causes the model to focus heavily on samples with wildly inaccurate predictions."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:77
msgid "**代价**：对异常值太敏感。如果数据里有一个极端异常点，MSE会为了讨好它而牺牲其他大部分样本的准确性。"
msgstr "**Cost**: Excessive sensitivity to outliers. If an extreme outlier exists in the dataset, MSE will sacrifice accuracy across most normal samples just to appease that single outlier."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:79
#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:128
msgid "数学形式"
msgstr "Mathematical Form"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:81
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\text{MSE} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n (y_i - \\hat{y}_i)^2"
msgstr "\\text{MSE} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n (y_i - \\hat{y}_i)^2"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:83
#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:112
#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:132
msgid "**特点**："
msgstr "**Characteristics**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:85
msgid "对**大误差惩罚更重**（平方增长）"
msgstr "**Heavier penalty on large errors** (quadratic growth)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:86
msgid "处处可导，便于梯度计算"
msgstr "Everywhere differentiable, facilitating gradient computation"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:87
msgid "对**异常值敏感**"
msgstr "**Sensitive to outliers**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:90
msgid "MSE损失函数形状"
msgstr "Shape of the MSE Loss Function"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:100
msgid "平均绝对误差（MAE）"
msgstr "Mean Absolute Error (MAE)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:102
msgid "一视同仁的\"公平裁判\""
msgstr "\"Fair Referee\" Treating All Errors Equally"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:104
msgid ""
"MSE 像是一个严厉的老师——小错误扣分少，大错误扣分特别多。而 MAE "
"更像是一个公平的裁判：偏差1就扣1分，偏差10就扣10分，**一视同仁**。"
msgstr ""
"MSE acts like a strict teacher—deducting few points for small mistakes but harsh penalties for big ones. MAE, on the other hand, acts like a fair referee: deducting 1 point for a deviation of 1, and 10 points for a deviation of 10, **treating all deviations equally**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:106
msgid ""
"**优势**：不会被个别极端值带偏。如果数据里有噪声或异常点（比如房价数据里混入了一个标价10亿的豪宅），MAE "
"不会为了这一个点而牺牲对其他正常房价的预测准确性。"
msgstr ""
"**Advantage**: Robust against individual extreme values. If noisy points or outliers exist in the data (such as a 1-billion-dollar mansion mixed into house price data), MAE will not sacrifice prediction accuracy on typical homes just to fit that single outlier."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:108
msgid ""
"**代价**：在误差为0的点不可导（像是一个尖角而非平滑的曲线），优化时会稍微麻烦一些。而且，因为它对所有错误一视同仁，对小错误的\"惩罚力度\"不够，收敛可能比"
" MSE 慢。"
msgstr ""
"**Cost**: Non-differentiable at zero error (forming a sharp V-shape rather than a smooth curve), making optimization slightly more involved. Furthermore, because it treats all errors equally, penalty on small errors is relatively mild, resulting in potentially slower convergence than MSE."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:110
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\text{MAE} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n |y_i - \\hat{y}_i|"
msgstr "\\text{MAE} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n |y_i - \\hat{y}_i|"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:114
msgid "对**异常值更鲁棒**（线性惩罚）"
msgstr "**More robust to outliers** (linear penalty)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:115
msgid "在零点**不可导**（可用次梯度）"
msgstr "**Non-differentiable at zero** (subgradient available)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:117
msgid "Huber损失（Smooth L1）"
msgstr "Huber Loss (Smooth L1)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:119
msgid "分情况的讨论"
msgstr "A Piecewise Compromise"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:121
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Huber 损失 {cite}`huber1964robust` 像一个有智慧的老师，懂得**因材施教**："
msgstr "Huber loss {cite}`huber1964robust` is like a wise teacher who tailors guidance to circumstance:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:123
msgid "**小错误时（误差 ≤ δ）**：像 MSE 一样严厉——\"这点小错都不能犯？给我好好学！\"平方惩罚让模型对小误差敏感，快速收敛。"
msgstr "**For small errors ($|\\text{error}| \\le \\delta$)**: Strict like MSE—quadratic penalty keeps the model sensitive to small errors for fast convergence."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:124
msgid "**大错误时（误差 > δ）**：像 MAE 一样理性——\"已经错这么远了，再骂也没用。\"线性惩罚避免异常值主导整个训练。"
msgstr "**For large errors ($|\\text{error}| > \\delta$)**: Rational like MAE—linear penalty prevents extreme outliers from dominating training gradients."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:126
msgid ""
"**参数 δ 的作用**：设定一个\"红线\"。偏差在红线内用平方（严格），超过红线改用线性（宽容）。目标检测任务常用 Huber "
"损失，因为位置偏差小时要精确定位，偏差大时可能是标注噪声，不必过分纠结。"
msgstr ""
"**Role of parameter $\\delta$**: Establishes a threshold (\"red line\"). Errors within $\\delta$ use quadratic penalty (strict), while errors beyond $\\delta$ switch to linear penalty (tolerant). Object detection tasks commonly use Huber loss because small bounding box errors demand precise localization, whereas large errors might reflect annotation noise that should not overwhelm training."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:130
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"L_\\delta(a) = \\begin{cases} \\frac{1}{2}a^2 & |a| \\leq \\delta \\\\ "
"\\delta(|a| - \\frac{1}{2}\\delta) & \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}"
msgstr ""
"L_\\delta(a) = \\begin{cases} \\frac{1}{2}a^2 & |a| \\leq \\delta \\\\ "
"\\delta(|a| - \\frac{1}{2}\\delta) & \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:134
msgid "小误差：MSE（平滑）"
msgstr "Small errors: MSE (smooth)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:135
msgid "大误差：MAE（鲁棒）"
msgstr "Large errors: MAE (robust)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:136
msgid "常用于目标检测等任务"
msgstr "Commonly used in object detection and related tasks"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:140
msgid "分类问题的损失函数"
msgstr "Loss Functions for Classification Problems"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:142
msgid "交叉熵损失（Cross-Entropy）"
msgstr "Cross-Entropy Loss"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:144
msgid "从编码角度理解"
msgstr "Understanding from an Information Coding Perspective"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:146
msgid "想象你要传递一条消息：\"这是一张猫的图片\"。如果只有10个可能的类别，最直接的编码方式是给每个类别分配一个编号（0-9）。但这种方式有问题：**如果模型预测\"狗\"的概率是80%而\"猫\"是20%，我们丢失了预测信心信息**。"
msgstr "Imagine transmitting a message: \"This is a picture of a cat.\" If there are only 10 possible classes, the most straightforward encoding is assigning an integer ID (0–9). But this approach has a flaw: **if the model predicts an 80% probability for \"dog\" and 20% for \"cat\", integer IDs discard all confidence information**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:148
msgid "更好的方式是使用**概率分布**作为编码。模型输出 $[0.1, 0.7, 0.05, ...]$ 表示对每个类别的信心。"
msgstr "A better approach uses a **probability distribution** as code, where model outputs like $[0.1, 0.7, 0.05, ...]$ express confidence across classes."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:150
msgid "**One-Hot编码**：将类别标签转换为向量，对应类别的位置为1，其余为0。"
msgstr "**One-Hot Encoding**: Converts categorical labels into vectors where the target class position is 1 and all others are 0."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:153
msgid "One-Hot编码示例"
msgstr "Example of One-Hot Encoding"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:178
msgid "**为什么叫\"One-Hot\"？**"
msgstr "**Why is it called \"One-Hot\"?**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:180
msgid "**One**：只有一个位置是1"
msgstr "**One**: Exactly one position contains a 1"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:181
msgid "**Hot**：这个位置\"激活\"（热），其余都是\"冷\"（0）"
msgstr "**Hot**: That single position is \"active\" (hot), while all others are \"cold\" (0)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:183
msgid "交叉熵公式"
msgstr "Cross-Entropy Formula"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:185
msgid "交叉熵衡量**用预测分布 $Q$ 来编码真实分布 $P$ 所需的平均信息量**："
msgstr "Cross-entropy measures the **average code length required when encoding true distribution $P$ using predicted distribution $Q$**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:187
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\text{CE}(P, Q) = -\\sum_{i} P(i) \\log Q(i)"
msgstr "\\text{CE}(P, Q) = -\\sum_{i} P(i) \\log Q(i)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:189
msgid "对于分类问题（$P$ 是one-hot编码），这简化为："
msgstr "For classification problems (where $P$ is one-hot encoded), this simplifies to:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:191
msgid "\\text{CE} = -\\log(\\hat{y}_{\\text{正确类别}})"
msgstr "\\text{CE} = -\\log(\\hat{y}_{\\text{correct class}})"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:193
msgid "**关键性质**："
msgstr "**Key Properties**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:195
msgid "预测越准（概率接近1），损失越低"
msgstr "More accurate predictions (probability closer to 1) yield lower loss"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:196
msgid "对**错误预测惩罚很大**（预测接近0时损失→∞）"
msgstr "**Heavy penalty for incorrect predictions** (loss $\\to \\infty$ as predicted probability $\\to 0$)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:197
msgid "与softmax配合，梯度形式简洁"
msgstr "Yields a remarkably clean gradient when combined with Softmax"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:200
msgid "交叉熵损失：惩罚错误预测"
msgstr "Cross-Entropy Loss: Penalizing Confident Wrong Predictions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:219
msgid "**为什么不用MSE做分类？**"
msgstr "**Why not use MSE for classification?**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:221
msgid "MSE在预测概率接近0或1时梯度很小，学习缓慢"
msgstr "MSE yields tiny gradients when predicted probabilities approach 0 or 1, slowing down learning"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:222
msgid "交叉熵在错误预测时提供更强的梯度信号"
msgstr "Cross-entropy provides much stronger gradient signals during confident mispredictions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:224
msgid "KL散度（Kullback-Leibler Divergence）"
msgstr "KL Divergence (Kullback-Leibler Divergence)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:226
msgid "直觉：额外的编码代价"
msgstr "Intuition: Extra Coding Penalty"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:228
msgid ""
"想象你有一个完美的天气预测模型 $P$（知道每天实际下雨的概率），但你只能用另一个模型 $Q$ 来做预测。KL散度衡量的是：**因为使用了不完美的"
" $Q$ 而不是真实的 $P$，你需要多传输多少信息**。"
msgstr ""
"Imagine you have a perfect weather forecasting model $P$ (knowing the actual daily probability of rain), but you must use another model $Q$ for predictions. KL divergence measures **how much extra information you need to transmit because you used imperfect model $Q$ instead of true distribution $P$**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:230
#, python-brace-format
msgid "D_{KL}(P \\| Q) = \\sum_{i} P(i) \\log \\frac{P(i)}{Q(i)}"
msgstr "D_{KL}(P \\| Q) = \\sum_{i} P(i) \\log \\frac{P(i)}{Q(i)}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:232
msgid "**直观例子**："
msgstr "**Intuitive Examples**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:234
msgid "如果 $Q = P$（预测完美），额外代价为0"
msgstr "If $Q = P$ (perfect prediction), the extra cost is 0"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:235
msgid "如果预测经常出错，代价就高"
msgstr "If predictions are frequently wrong, the extra cost is high"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:236
msgid "**非对称**：用 $Q$ 近似 $P$ 的代价 ≠ 用 $P$ 近似 $Q$ 的代价"
msgstr "**Asymmetric**: Cost of approximating $P$ with $Q$ $\\neq$ cost of approximating $Q$ with $P$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:238
msgid "与交叉熵的关系"
msgstr "Relationship to Cross-Entropy"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:240
msgid ""
"\\underbrace{\\text{CrossEntropy}(P, Q)}_{\\text{总编码长度}} = "
"\\underbrace{H(P)}_{\\text{最优编码长度}} + \\underbrace{D_{KL}(P \\| "
"Q)}_{\\text{额外代价}}"
msgstr ""
"\\underbrace{\\text{CrossEntropy}(P, Q)}_{\\text{Total code length}} = "
"\\underbrace{H(P)}_{\\text{Optimal code length}} + \\underbrace{D_{KL}(P \\| "
"Q)}_{\\text{Extra penalty}}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:242
msgid "其中 $H(P)$ 是分布 $P$ 的**熵**（信息论中最小可能编码长度）。因为真实分布 $P$ 是固定的，$H(P)$ 是常数。因此："
msgstr "where $H(P)$ is the **entropy** of distribution $P$ (the minimum possible code length in information theory). Since the ground-truth distribution $P$ is fixed, $H(P)$ is constant. Therefore:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:244
msgid "**最小化交叉熵 = 最小化KL散度 = 让预测分布尽可能接近真实分布**"
msgstr "**Minimizing Cross-Entropy = Minimizing KL Divergence = Driving predicted distribution as close as possible to the true distribution**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:246
msgid "应用场景"
msgstr "Application Scenarios"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:248
msgid "**变分自编码器（VAE）**：约束潜在变量 $z$ 的分布接近标准正态分布"
msgstr "**Variational Autoencoders (VAEs)**: Constraining the latent distribution $z$ to match a standard normal distribution"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:249
msgid "**知识蒸馏**：让小模型学习大模型的\"软预测\"（概率分布），而非硬标签"
msgstr "**Knowledge Distillation**: Teaching a small model to match the \"soft predictions\" (probability distributions) of a teacher model rather than hard labels"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:250
msgid "**强化学习**：限制策略更新幅度，防止模型突变"
msgstr "**Reinforcement Learning**: Constraining policy update step sizes to prevent drastic policy drift"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:254
msgid "损失函数选择指南"
msgstr "Loss Function Selection Guide"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:256
msgid "损失函数选择参考"
msgstr "Reference for Selecting Loss Functions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:260
msgid "**问题类型**"
msgstr "**Problem Type**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:261
msgid "**推荐损失**"
msgstr "**Recommended Loss**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:262
msgid "**优势**"
msgstr "**Advantages**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:263
msgid "**注意事项**"
msgstr "**Caveats**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:264
msgid "回归问题"
msgstr "Regression problem"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:265
msgid "MSE / MAE"
msgstr "MSE / MAE"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:266
msgid "MSE光滑可导，MAE鲁棒"
msgstr "MSE is smooth and differentiable; MAE is robust"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:267
msgid "数据有异常值时选MAE"
msgstr "Choose MAE when dataset contains outliers"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:268
msgid "回归（需鲁棒性）"
msgstr "Regression (demanding robustness)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:269
msgid "Huber损失"
msgstr "Huber loss"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:270
msgid "结合两者优点"
msgstr "Combines benefits of both MSE and MAE"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:271
msgid "需要调超参数$\\delta$"
msgstr "Requires tuning hyperparameter $\\delta$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/loss-functions.md:272
